# Copy this file to .env.local (already gitignored) and fill in your own
# values. Nothing here is required for the app to work — every feature that
# reads one of these is inert, not broken, when it's left unset.

# Google Drive integration's OAuth Client ID (src/lib/drive/). One-time
# setup, done by you, not this app:
#   1. https://console.cloud.google.com/ → create (or pick) a project.
#   2. APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen → configure it (External is
#      fine for a personal/single-user app; you don't need to publish it,
#      just add your own Google account as a test user).
#   3. APIs & Services → Enabled APIs → enable the "Google Drive API".
#   4. APIs & Services → Credentials → Create Credentials → OAuth client ID
#      → Application type "Web application".
#   5. Under "Authorized JavaScript origins", add every origin you'll open
#      the app from — e.g. http://localhost:5173 for `npm run dev` and
#      https://maat-apps.github.io for the deployed site. No redirect URI
#      is needed (this app uses the token client, not the redirect flow).
#   6. Paste the generated Client ID below.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
